+# Why Session Replay Is Empty on the New UI
+
+## Root Cause
+
+In `posthog_flutter`, enabling `config.sessionReplay = true` in `PostHogConfig` (`lib/analytics.dart`) is necessary but not sufficient for Flutter session replay to record the screen. The root application widget must also be wrapped in `PostHogWidget`.
+
+`PostHogWidget` places a `RepaintBoundary` and screenshot/interaction capture layer around the Flutter widget tree so `posthog_flutter` can capture frames, apply text/image masking (`maskAllTexts` / `maskAllImages`), and forward replay snapshots to the native PostHog SDK.
+
+- **Old UI (`lib/legacy_app.dart`):** Wraps `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`, so session replay snapshots are captured and uploaded normally.
+- **New UI (`lib/new_app.dart`):** Returned `MaterialApp.router(...)` directly without wrapping it in `PostHogWidget`. Because `Posthog().setup(config)` and `PosthogObserver()` were still configured, custom events (`loan_amount_changed`, `application_submitted`, etc.) and screen navigation events continued to arrive in PostHog, but no visual session replay frames were ever captured.
+
+## Fix
+
+Wrapped `MaterialApp.router` inside `PostHogWidget` in `lib/new_app.dart` (matching `lib/legacy_app.dart`):
+
+```dart
+@override
+Widget build(BuildContext context) {
+  return PostHogWidget(
+    child: MaterialApp.router(
+      title: 'Loanly',
+      theme: ThemeData(
+        colorSchemeSeed: Colors.indigo,
+        useMaterial3: true,
+      ),
+      routerConfig: _router,
+    ),
+  );
+}
+```
